{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"**As of November 6, 2026:**\n\n- **Eligible:** Registered open-end management-company ETFs—index-based or actively managed—that satisfy Rule 6c-11’s daily portfolio transparency, disclosure, basket, recordkeeping and other conditions.\n- **Leveraged/inverse ETFs:** Also eligible. The 2020 Rule 18f-4 amendments removed their original exclusion from 6c-11. They must separately satisfy applicable derivatives-risk-management and VaR requirements, including special leveraged/inverse provisions. Narrow grandfathering for certain existing funds is not blanket permission for new 3× ETFs.\n- **Separate exemptive relief needed:** UIT ETFs, nontransparent/semitransparent ETFs, and ETFs structured as share classes of multiclass funds.\n- **Outside this framework:** Commodity/grantor trusts, commodity pools and ETNs follow different regulatory regimes; they are not automatically candidates for 6c-11 relief.\n\n**Worth knowing:** [Rule 6c-11](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/section-270.6c-11) provides ETF operational exemptions; [Rule 18f-4](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/section-270.18f-4) governs derivatives use. Neither substitutes for the other."}}
